WEBVTT

01:30.520 --> 01:32.980
Episode 5: Berliner Mystery

01:36.400 --> 01:37.570
Osanai-san.

01:39.660 --> 01:40.870
Osanai-san?

01:42.200 --> 01:43.240
Kobato-kun.

01:47.500 --> 01:50.580
What did I do wrong?

01:51.000 --> 01:53.750
Called to the guidance 
counselor's office again?

01:54.340 --> 01:56.720
I'll be at Humpty Dumpty.

02:04.520 --> 02:06.520
<b>Newspaper Club Room</b>

02:20.360 --> 02:21.620
Um...

02:22.030 --> 02:23.870
I guess you're busy.

02:23.870 --> 02:26.040
Oh, it's Jogoro. What's up?

02:26.500 --> 02:28.540
I brought the surveys.

02:28.540 --> 02:30.670
Oh, okay. Good timing.

02:32.170 --> 02:33.540
Say, Jogoro...

02:34.170 --> 02:38.470
Apparently, there's this snack 
called a Berliner Pfannkuchen.

02:38.920 --> 02:41.220
A Ber... What?

02:41.220 --> 02:43.720
Berliner Pfannkuchen.

02:43.720 --> 02:47.220
<b>Funato High School Newspaper Club</b>

02:43.720 --> 02:47.220
<b>Funato High School Newspaper Club</b>

02:43.720 --> 02:47.220
Members Wanted

02:43.720 --> 02:47.220
Topic for this month's article:
German bakery opened up nearby.
Cover their Berliner Pfannkuchen.

02:44.760 --> 02:47.890
It's a baked pastry from Germany. 
Berlin's known for them.

02:49.440 --> 02:51.480
It's filled with jam.

02:51.480 --> 02:55.110
There's a game where 
you make a bunch of them,

02:55.110 --> 02:58.490
but fill some with mustard,
and you see who ends up with those ones.

03:01.490 --> 03:05.530
A German bakery opened up recently.

03:05.530 --> 03:09.710
We thought it'd be fun to go external for once,
 so we asked them if we could do an article.

03:10.620 --> 03:14.040
And for the heck of it, 
we figured we'd play that game.

03:14.040 --> 03:17.760
And the one who got the mustard one
 would write the article.

03:18.340 --> 03:22.720
I'd appreciate it if you would 
get to the point already.

03:22.720 --> 03:25.640
We all played the game together.

03:25.640 --> 03:27.890
But everyone says they weren't it.

03:28.520 --> 03:31.310
Do you know what that means, Jogoro?

03:34.900 --> 03:38.650
Uh, well, I'm Kobato from Class 2-A. 
Nice to meet you.

03:39.230 --> 03:44.030
So the pastries were split between four. 
And there were four on the plate.

03:44.570 --> 03:48.370
Only one had mustard in it, correct?

03:48.370 --> 03:49.830
That's right.

03:49.830 --> 03:56.130
Myself, Monchi, Makishima, 
and Itsukaichi here had one each.

03:56.130 --> 03:58.960
And we all say we didn't 
get the mustard one.

03:59.460 --> 04:01.670
We haven't touched the plate since.

04:02.800 --> 04:03.840
Thanks.

04:07.510 --> 04:09.060
What's up with this fridge?

04:09.060 --> 04:11.810
Oh, it's practically a cupboard.

04:12.480 --> 04:13.940
It doesn't even have power.

04:16.020 --> 04:18.940
Could you tell me the size
and shape of this pastry?

04:20.230 --> 04:24.360
We needed photos for the article, 
so we took these before we ate them.

04:24.360 --> 04:26.200
They're pretty small.

04:26.660 --> 04:28.700
Apparently, they're normally bigger.

04:28.700 --> 04:32.750
They gave us some child-size ones 
they're experimenting with.

04:32.750 --> 04:34.710
Was there anything else you noticed?

04:36.420 --> 04:39.290
There were small holes 
in the base of the pastries.

04:39.290 --> 04:41.840
Presumably from when 
they were filled up with jam.

04:42.380 --> 04:45.130
We think the mustard must have
 been injected that way, too.

04:45.470 --> 04:46.720
I see.

04:47.970 --> 04:50.720
You had them just earlier, right?

04:50.720 --> 04:53.810
Yeah. Just after four thirty or thereabouts.

04:53.810 --> 04:56.400
Was there anyone else around?

04:56.400 --> 04:59.860
It was just the four of us here 
at the time we ate them.

05:01.400 --> 05:04.860
So there was someone else 
here at a <i>different</i> time?

05:04.860 --> 05:07.610
Yeah. The club president, Seba-san.

05:07.610 --> 05:10.080
He's the one who brought the pastries.

05:10.580 --> 05:12.120
Left before I got here, though.

05:12.490 --> 05:16.620
Seba-san's band has a concert today.
 He's the vocalist.

05:17.000 --> 05:22.000
So no other third party has been in here
 aside from this "Seba-san" guy?

05:22.000 --> 05:24.010
Not that I've seen, at least.

05:30.760 --> 05:32.220
Kengo, a moment.

05:33.640 --> 05:37.020
To be honest, I can't imagine anyone 
would have a motive to do this.

05:37.350 --> 05:40.690
They'd have to write the article 
if they got the mustard one, right?

05:40.690 --> 05:43.400
It'd simply mean they'd be assigned this story.

05:43.400 --> 05:45.900
The rest of us would write different articles.

05:47.320 --> 05:51.370
Maybe someone <i>really</i> didn't want 
to write about the pastry.

05:52.120 --> 05:57.710
It isn't mandatory. We have another first-year
 who isn't participating, either.

05:57.710 --> 06:00.330
What's his reason for not taking part?

06:01.710 --> 06:06.420
"I don't want to write such 
a sophomoric article," he said.

06:07.170 --> 06:10.090
A cocky kid named Urino.

06:10.800 --> 06:14.260
Also, do you really <i>need</i> to know 
who got the mustard one?

06:14.260 --> 06:17.020
Why not just do rock-paper-scissors 
to assign the article?

06:19.140 --> 06:22.730
To be honest, Monchi and Makishima 
aren't getting along too well.

06:23.020 --> 06:26.650
We need to find out the truth or 
they might end up calling each other liars,

06:26.650 --> 06:29.030
and take the whole newspaper 
club down with them.

06:29.610 --> 06:33.910
And just to be clear, 
you didn't get it, right, Kengo?

06:34.370 --> 06:35.120
Nope.

06:35.950 --> 06:38.750
So? Who was it?

06:38.750 --> 06:40.330
I don't know just yet.

06:40.750 --> 06:44.210
But there are four possible reasons
 for no one speaking up.

06:44.800 --> 06:48.420
First: there was never any mustard.

06:49.430 --> 06:53.850
Second: one pastry had mustard, 
but the person didn't notice.

06:55.100 --> 06:57.860
Third: someone got the mustard,

06:57.860 --> 07:00.640
but there's a reason they don't want to admit it.

07:02.020 --> 07:05.440
Fourth: third-party interference.

07:05.440 --> 07:08.650
I doubt that. There are four of us.

07:08.650 --> 07:10.650
And there were four pastries.

07:10.650 --> 07:13.660
I was here writing an article the whole time.

07:13.660 --> 07:15.870
I would've noticed if someone had come in.

07:15.870 --> 07:18.830
By "here," do you mean 
specifically in that seat?

07:18.830 --> 07:20.410
<i>That</i> seat.

07:20.870 --> 07:23.790
There's no way I wouldn't have noticed.

07:23.790 --> 07:25.790
I don't see a chair.

07:25.790 --> 07:28.670
Makishima-san and I 
are using them right now.

07:30.170 --> 07:33.430
Monchi was definitely 
writing when I arrived.

07:33.930 --> 07:37.470
Was Monchi-kun seated 
facing the center of the room?

07:37.470 --> 07:38.850
Or towards the window?

07:42.310 --> 07:44.690
His side was facing the window.

07:46.150 --> 07:47.780
Which means...

07:48.400 --> 07:51.200
someone in this group must
 have gotten the mustard.

07:51.610 --> 07:54.320
Did you have the mustard 
filling done at the shop?

07:54.700 --> 07:57.450
Seba-san would have gotten 
the home ec club to do it.

07:58.790 --> 08:02.580
Also, does this plate belong 
to the newspaper club?

08:02.580 --> 08:05.880
No. I think it was borrowed 
from the home ec club.

08:05.880 --> 08:08.250
I think we'll need to find out.

08:09.460 --> 08:13.340
Meanwhile, could you each write 
your thoughts on how the pastry tasted,

08:13.340 --> 08:15.050
and make sure no one else sees?

08:18.470 --> 08:21.480
<b>Home Economics Room</b>

08:20.060 --> 08:21.480
Hello.

08:21.480 --> 08:23.100
Could I ask you something?

08:23.100 --> 08:24.190
What is it?

08:24.190 --> 08:26.480
I'm here from the newspaper club.

08:28.230 --> 08:30.480
Ah. How was it?

08:31.070 --> 08:32.400
How was what?

08:35.280 --> 08:38.120
Aren't you here about the pastry?

08:39.200 --> 08:43.040
Seba-san definitely 
went to the home ec club.

08:43.410 --> 08:43.870
Sweeter than I expected.
Blueberry Jam?
Dojima

08:43.750 --> 08:46.670
Before I go on, let's see what 
everyone wrote about the pastries.

08:43.870 --> 08:44.500
Sweeter than I expected.
Blueberry Jam?
Dojima

08:44.500 --> 08:45.250
Sweeter than I expected.
Blueberry Jam?
Dojima

08:47.920 --> 08:50.420
Did someone get the mustard 
without knowing it?

08:49.130 --> 08:51.920
<b>There's the fluffy outer layer,
and in it a burst of really sweet jam.
Two varieties of berry jam, maybe?
Makishima</b>

08:49.130 --> 08:51.920
<b>It was nice and sweet.
It was a lot of jam.
Itsukaichi</b>

08:49.130 --> 08:51.920
<b>It was really, really sweet.
Got my hands all messy.
Monchi</b>

08:52.420 --> 08:53.920
Nope.

08:54.470 --> 08:55.800
In other words...

08:56.530 --> 08:59.010
Someone has to be lying.

08:59.970 --> 09:03.560
We all know Berliners are sweet.

09:03.560 --> 09:06.310
I-I wrote that because I really liked it.

09:06.310 --> 09:08.900
I wasn't necessarily 
talking to you, Itsukaichi.

09:10.020 --> 09:12.280
Who <i>were</i> you talking to, then?

09:12.280 --> 09:16.610
If you ask me, it's <i>more</i> suspicious 
that you could supposedly tell

09:16.610 --> 09:20.370
it was berry jam just 
from that one small donut.

09:17.410 --> 09:20.370
<b>There's the fluffy outer layer,
\hand in it a burst of really sweet jam.
\h\hTwo varieties of berry jam, maybe?
\h\h\hMakishima</b>

09:20.370 --> 09:22.790
It was clearly berry jam.

09:22.790 --> 09:25.160
That's what I thought, too.

09:26.370 --> 09:28.130
Oh, but you see...

09:28.560 --> 09:31.880
There was no mustard 
in any of the pastries.

09:33.090 --> 09:34.880
Yup, not a smidgen of it.

09:34.880 --> 09:38.010
I was told you'd put mustard in it.

09:38.680 --> 09:41.010
I guess I should tell you everything.

09:41.720 --> 09:44.520
I asked Seba what kind of mustard to use.

09:44.850 --> 09:48.270
He said, "Whatever's fine. 
Just make sure it's hot." What a pain.

09:48.650 --> 09:51.320
Mustard isn't that hot, you see.

09:51.320 --> 09:52.320
Makes sense.

09:52.820 --> 09:55.900
So I asked Seba to choose 
between mustard or something spicy.

09:55.900 --> 09:57.910
He told me to make it spicy.

09:57.910 --> 09:59.240
So I did.

10:00.200 --> 10:01.830
Habanero sauce.

10:02.280 --> 10:03.620
It's hot as hell.

10:05.370 --> 10:08.750
Well, that's a surprise, for sure, 
but does it change anything?

10:09.670 --> 10:17.260
I'm still convinced there's a nonzero chance 
the person who got the sauce didn't realize it.

10:17.800 --> 10:19.550
What are you talking about?

10:19.550 --> 10:21.390
Taste disorders.

10:21.390 --> 10:24.140
How about we do an experiment?

10:24.970 --> 10:26.600
Let's do a lick test.

10:30.060 --> 10:33.230
I think we have paper plates somewhere.

10:33.230 --> 10:35.570
We did. Where did we put them?

10:35.570 --> 10:37.400
Oh, uh, on top of the fridge.

10:39.780 --> 10:42.320
Please leave your surveys
 in the basket.
The snacks are a token of gratitude.
Feel free to take them.

10:40.360 --> 10:41.320
What's this?

10:41.740 --> 10:46.120
Oh, it's a modest gift for the students
 delivering the survey results.

10:46.950 --> 10:49.040
Pretty classy choice.

10:50.920 --> 10:52.460
Don't get any in your eyes.

10:52.880 --> 10:56.090
I was told it's dangerous to even 
touch your eyes after you've licked it.

10:56.710 --> 10:59.590
All right. Let's get this over with.

10:59.590 --> 11:01.720
Jogoro, give the signal.

11:01.720 --> 11:04.720
U-Uh, okay. Ready...

11:07.980 --> 11:08.850
Go.

11:13.610 --> 11:15.110
Man, that's hot.

11:15.110 --> 11:16.650
Unbearably so?

11:18.400 --> 11:19.740
Jogoro, there's no way.

11:20.280 --> 11:23.120
Who the hell puts this stuff in pastry?

11:23.530 --> 11:24.660
Me.

11:24.660 --> 11:28.330
Was Seba-san watching as 
you injected the habanero sauce?

11:28.870 --> 11:32.750
He wasn't. He also said he had 
no idea which one was spiked.

11:33.130 --> 11:37.460
Do you have any idea why 
no one seems to have gotten it?

11:38.960 --> 11:42.130
I definitely put habanero sauce in there.

11:42.130 --> 11:47.140
There's no way someone 
would've eaten it and not reacted.

11:47.640 --> 11:50.810
We have learned three things
 from this experiment.

11:51.230 --> 11:54.440
First, this habanero sauce is extremely hot.

11:55.110 --> 12:00.030
Next, there was no one out of the four of you
who wouldn't have felt the heat.

12:00.650 --> 12:02.200
And lastly...

12:02.200 --> 12:05.160
Ah, screw it! It's just some damn pastry!

12:05.160 --> 12:07.530
Do you really want this all to go to waste?

12:08.040 --> 12:12.040
Who was the one who decided 
to do an article on this pastry?

12:12.460 --> 12:14.750
I proposed it in an editorial meeting.

12:14.750 --> 12:16.920
Seba-san liked the idea, 
so we went ahead with it.

12:17.210 --> 12:21.170
And why do you believe Seba-san 
ended up going to get the pastries?

12:21.510 --> 12:25.550
He can't handle spicy stuff, 
so he didn't take part in the game.

12:26.220 --> 12:31.810
Also, he felt guilty about not showing up
 to the club because of his concert.

12:32.140 --> 12:36.020
He offered to go get the pastries 
as a way of making up for it.

12:36.020 --> 12:39.440
As bumbling as he seems, 
he takes good care of us.

12:39.820 --> 12:43.650
He always give us advice when 
we get stuck on our writing and stuff.

12:45.070 --> 12:48.830
Seba-san went to get 
the pastries after school,

12:48.830 --> 12:53.250
then had one spiked with habanero sauce
 before placing them all on a plate.

12:54.250 --> 12:57.750
And he'd left by the time you ate them.

12:59.210 --> 13:01.920
Who was the first one 
to come to the clubroom?

13:01.920 --> 13:03.220
Me.

13:03.510 --> 13:04.800
What time did you get here?

13:05.340 --> 13:07.850
I think it was a little after half three.

13:07.850 --> 13:10.100
So you met Seba-san, right?

13:10.470 --> 13:11.430
Yeah.

13:11.810 --> 13:14.440
He tapped me on the shoulder 
out of nowhere. Freaked me out.

13:15.480 --> 13:16.730
What time was that?

13:16.730 --> 13:20.940
I don't remember. I wasn't watching 
the clock while I was writing.

13:20.940 --> 13:25.490
That three-part article we've been 
doing since last week, right? Are you stuck?

13:25.490 --> 13:28.320
Yeah. I was struggling with how to write it.

13:28.320 --> 13:29.910
I'm done now, though.

13:30.700 --> 13:34.290
Seba-san was holding the plate 
with the pastries, right?

13:34.790 --> 13:38.710
Nope. The pastries were 
already on this table.

13:38.710 --> 13:40.460
Who came into the room next?

13:41.550 --> 13:42.880
Me.

13:43.420 --> 13:45.720
I met Seba-san, too.

13:45.720 --> 13:49.470
I asked him if he'd been here long, 
and he said he'd just gotten here.

13:49.470 --> 13:53.020
He said he was sorry he couldn't 
stick around since he had his concert.

13:53.520 --> 13:55.350
That was quarter past four.

13:56.640 --> 14:00.020
So it would've been right 
after he'd talked to Monchi.

14:00.900 --> 14:05.820
The survey submission box was on the table.

14:05.820 --> 14:07.820
I took a few and read through them.

14:10.030 --> 14:11.870
Which seat were you in?

14:11.870 --> 14:13.160
That one.

14:13.660 --> 14:14.660
And then?

14:17.080 --> 14:23.420
I tidied up the table so we could 
get a good photo of the pastries.

14:25.920 --> 14:28.630
Who came into the room next?

14:28.630 --> 14:29.840
Me.

14:29.840 --> 14:32.140
I don't remember what time I got here.

14:32.600 --> 14:37.430
Monchi and Itsukaichi were already here, 
but I didn't see Seba-san.

14:37.850 --> 14:39.480
Was there anything else of note?

14:40.650 --> 14:45.230
Oh, a first-year came to deliver 
the surveys, so I took them off him.

14:45.230 --> 14:50.070
I thanked him and offered him 
the snacks, but he declined.

14:47.440 --> 14:52.700
Please leave your surveys
 in the basket.
The snacks are a token of gratitude.
Feel free to take them.

14:50.910 --> 14:52.700
What about the survey forms?

14:53.700 --> 14:55.450
I handed them to Itsukaichi.

14:55.740 --> 14:57.870
And where's the box?

14:57.870 --> 14:59.920
Behind Dojima.

15:01.080 --> 15:02.880
You put it there?

15:03.840 --> 15:05.380
Was there anything else?

15:07.670 --> 15:10.880
You were the last to arrive, right, Kengo?
 What time was that?

15:11.470 --> 15:15.220
I remember thinking I had 
some time until half four.

15:15.760 --> 15:18.930
The other three were here when I arrived.

15:18.930 --> 15:21.190
And I saw the pastries on the table.

15:24.820 --> 15:27.650
See? Nothing suspicious, right?

15:28.780 --> 15:34.490
Would anyone really have pretended with 
ill intent that they didn't get the spiked one?

15:34.490 --> 15:35.410
Say what?

15:36.790 --> 15:40.960
I think no one ate it.

15:41.960 --> 15:43.580
That doesn't make sense.

15:43.580 --> 15:47.130
You were the one who confirmed 
one of them had habanero sauce in it.

15:47.130 --> 15:48.050
Yeah.

15:48.050 --> 15:51.260
Yet you also believe no one ate it?

15:53.430 --> 15:55.600
You're right. It's absurd.

15:56.010 --> 16:01.600
But it's even more absurd to think someone 
could have eaten it with everyone present.

16:01.600 --> 16:02.560
How come?

16:03.770 --> 16:07.940
There's no way anyone could have pretended 
they didn't consume a sauce this hot.

16:05.940 --> 16:08.690
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

16:05.940 --> 16:08.690
m 30 65 l 15 95 45 95

16:05.940 --> 16:08.690
<b>!</b>

16:05.940 --> 16:08.690
<b>Extremely spicy. Please consult
a physician if you get any in your 
eyes. Keep out of reach of children.</b>

16:08.690 --> 16:14.450
Someone could have swallowed it if they 
were absolutely intent on fighting through it.

16:14.450 --> 16:16.450
No, that's impossible, too.

16:17.030 --> 16:20.870
All four of you thought 
it'd have mustard inside.

16:21.540 --> 16:24.830
So if any of you had gotten 
that habanero sauce instead...

16:24.830 --> 16:26.840
It would have been impossible to endure.

16:27.130 --> 16:29.840
Where did the spiked one go, then?

16:30.130 --> 16:32.050
Who would have eaten it?

16:32.050 --> 16:34.680
First of all, there were only four pastries.

16:34.680 --> 16:36.220
About that...

16:37.720 --> 16:41.680
Seba-san knew Urino-kun 
wasn't participating, right?

16:43.140 --> 16:44.810
Did anyone contact him?

16:44.810 --> 16:46.360
I didn't.

16:48.480 --> 16:50.940
Seriously? No one did?

16:50.940 --> 16:52.820
Neither did you, Monchi.

16:52.820 --> 16:56.360
<i>You're</i> the one who's always chatting it up
 with Seba-san about mundane stuff.

16:56.360 --> 16:59.660
Huh? You constantly cause him trouble, too.

16:59.660 --> 17:00.790
No, <i>you</i> do!

16:59.910 --> 17:01.160
Guys, stop.

17:00.790 --> 17:01.790
No, it's <i>you</i>.

17:02.370 --> 17:08.920
By the way, do you remember what Monchi-kun 
said earlier about Seba-san coming in here?

17:09.550 --> 17:12.550
That he freaked out when 
he got tapped on the shoulder.

17:13.470 --> 17:14.550
In other words...

17:16.550 --> 17:21.310
His assertion that he would've noticed 
if someone had entered wasn't quite true.

17:24.390 --> 17:27.020
If Monchi-kun wouldn't
 have noticed a visitor,

17:27.020 --> 17:29.820
it stands to reason 
Seba-san might not, either.

17:29.820 --> 17:31.780
That's a stretch.

17:31.780 --> 17:35.450
The chances of someone noticing 
ought to be higher with two in here.

17:36.160 --> 17:39.780
Monchi-kun was writing 
from around half three.

17:40.280 --> 17:44.460
Kengo says it was the three-part article 
he'd been working on since last week.

17:44.970 --> 17:49.000
Monchi-kun said, "Yeah, I was 
struggling with how to write it,"

17:49.000 --> 17:50.880
but said he was done now.

17:52.550 --> 17:57.970
In other words, Monchi was having a hard time 
with the article, but got it done earlier.

17:58.640 --> 18:01.720
So what was Seba-san like again?

18:02.470 --> 18:06.350
He always give us advice 
when we get stuck on our writing.

18:08.060 --> 18:12.150
Monchi-kun was getting advice from 
Seba-san on how to write the article.

18:12.980 --> 18:17.030
This is just a guess, 
but was Seba-san sitting down, too?

18:17.820 --> 18:20.490
I didn't mention it 'cause 
I didn't think it was a big deal.

18:20.990 --> 18:25.290
In other words, when Seba-san told 
Itsukaichi-kun he'd just gotten here,

18:25.290 --> 18:28.920
he meant roughly within 
a span of several minutes.

18:30.000 --> 18:32.380
So how long exactly?

18:32.670 --> 18:34.000
Dunno.

18:34.000 --> 18:35.590
Maybe five minutes?

18:35.590 --> 18:38.510
It's possible that both 
Monchi-kun and Seba-san

18:38.510 --> 18:41.760
failed to notice someone else 
entering in the meantime.

18:42.390 --> 18:44.060
Is that fair to say?

18:44.600 --> 18:46.390
Suit yourself.

18:46.770 --> 18:50.980
Anyway, given all the 
information we have so far,

18:50.980 --> 18:53.900
we can suppose there were five pastries.

18:54.730 --> 18:55.900
Five?

18:56.490 --> 18:58.360
One for Urino-kun.

18:58.360 --> 19:00.200
If no one had contacted him,

19:00.200 --> 19:03.700
Seba-san would've assumed Urino-kun 
was participating in the game.

19:04.280 --> 19:06.040
That does make sense.

19:06.410 --> 19:10.250
And there's a five-minute blank in our 
knowledge of what happened in the room.

19:10.750 --> 19:14.410
So who could have eaten
 the habanero donut?

19:16.320 --> 19:21.850
We can assume the culprit acted without 
ever talking to Monchi-kun or Seba-san.

19:22.450 --> 19:25.930
The pastries were prepared for the article.

19:26.260 --> 19:31.700
It doesn't make sense for a member to eat 
the extra one just because it was unclaimed.

19:32.940 --> 19:35.180
That's true.

19:35.860 --> 19:37.570
But have you noticed, Jogoro?

19:38.350 --> 19:40.100
We don't have any suspects now.

19:42.330 --> 19:43.520
Maybe it was Urino.

19:43.520 --> 19:45.700
He talked to me before he went home.

19:46.860 --> 19:51.110
Kengo, can you describe how 
the pastries and the plate looked

19:51.110 --> 19:54.080
in the five-minute blank 
before Seba-san left the room?

19:55.590 --> 20:00.780
Just like this. Of course, the pastries
 were there in the moment you're describing.

20:01.690 --> 20:03.380
But it wasn't like this.

20:04.220 --> 20:09.530
The pastries and the plate were 
only there <i>after</i> the five-minute blank.

20:10.600 --> 20:15.400
We know this because Itsukaichi-kun, 
who came in just as Seba-san was leaving,

20:15.400 --> 20:18.260
tidied up the table 
to prepare it for the photos.

20:20.150 --> 20:23.110
The plate of pastries 
in the five-minute blank...

20:24.500 --> 20:26.350
was placed like this.

20:27.000 --> 20:28.340
Of course!

20:28.340 --> 20:31.150
This bowl was here next to the pastries.

20:31.580 --> 20:33.980
Kengo, the survey submission box, please.

20:33.980 --> 20:34.690
Right.

20:40.680 --> 20:43.770
It isn't just the newspaper club 
members that come into this room.

20:43.770 --> 20:47.910
For example, I'm in here, 
and Makishima-san met that male first-year.

20:47.910 --> 20:50.830
We came here to deliver the surveys.

20:51.260 --> 20:56.050
And there's no reason to assume 
it was just the two of us.

20:58.900 --> 21:01.900
Class 2-C

21:04.720 --> 21:05.950
What's wrong with you?

21:05.950 --> 21:06.910
I see now.

21:07.450 --> 21:08.990
So <i>that's</i> what happened.
